 python tools/run_predict_direct_one_shot_latency_v1.py --mode reconcile --run-dir "<run_dir>"
 ```
 
+Recovery writes under `<run_dir>/reconciliation/<new-id>/` and preserves the
+original run. It waits for a canonical native wallet event or its observation
+deadline, then makes at most one REST order snapshot request. A throttled read
+does not trigger an immediate retry or an order resubmission. Known ACK,
+settlement-success and confirmed FILLED evidence take precedence over a later
+query error in the summary. An ACK with unresolved reconciliation is reported
+as `PREDICT_ACK_OBSERVED_RECONCILIATION_INCOMPLETE`.
+
 The timeline captures receipt before JSON parsing, fixed decision, amount
 calculation, SDK build/signing, guard persistence, HTTP call, body write, response
 headers/JSON, canonical Predict ACK, native `orderAccepted`, settlement submitted,
